  "register": "filter",
  "node": "python",
  "path": "local_nodes.podcast_prepare_clip",
  "prefix": "podcast_prepare_clip",
  "description": [
    "Resolves one clip of an analysed episode (an analysis candidate, a Prompt Director candidate, a saved edit version, or explicit start/end) into a render-ready plan: extracts the interval, aligns word timestamps with faster-whisper, snaps the boundaries to word edges, plans filler/pause edits with safety rules (smart / cut / mute / keep, per-cut restore), fits the duration to the requested target (natural / strict / maximum \u2014 never through a word) and writes analysis/clips/<id>/plan.json + compliance.json. The generic render spec goes out on the text lane (for speaker_framing / media_render) and, when a video listener is wired, a small copy of the clip goes out on the video lane for the stock frame grabber + pose estimator (phase 2 layouts). Chat context lines: 'project:', 'clip:', optional 'start:', 'end:', 'title:', 'captions:', 'layouts:', 'fillers:', 'silences:', 'duration:', 'mode:', 'version:', 'restore:', 'layout: auto|solo|stacked|screen|full|original', 'model: tiny|base|small|medium|large-v3' (word-timing model override for this render), 'subject: p2'. Render settings for the spec it emits: 'render_mode: preview | export', size, layouts, fps, crf, preset, captions, sidecars (or 'render: preview|export' in the question)."
  ],
  "icon": "podcast-prepare-clip.svg",
  "documentation": "https://docs.rocketride.org",
  "lanes": {
    "questions": [
      "text",
      "video"
    ]
  },
  "preconfig": {
    "default": "default",
    "profiles": {
      "default": {
        "model": "medium",
        "language": "en",
        "pad_seconds": 2,
        "filler_policy": "smart",
        "silence_policy": "tighten",
        "caption_preset": "classic",
